assess('06-synthesis.md','sec:SYNTHESIS-COVARIANCE-EXAMPLE',['p60','p73','p75','p83','p87'],'one rises whenever the other falls','Opposite tuning slopes give oppositely signed expected-rate changes.','one shared position displacement','two cells’ expected firing rates','raises one and lowers the other','with only the common source, correlation is minus one','retain','The direct plain explanation interprets the calculated negative covariance. It is not a claim about inhibition.','Retain the explicit single-source and added-private-noise conditions, as well as the chosen baseline in the figure. The sidecar summary should stop before an absent equation rather than end with “are.”','Correlation, covariance and local tuning slope have prior teaching. “Example:” is the guide’s callout heading form, so the colon is intentional.','Numerical slopes, D and interval appear before the arithmetic.','The heading already gives the observed consequence in this example.','The final measurement requirement follows from the difference between demonstrating a possible covariance pattern and establishing its cause.')
assess('06-synthesis.md','sec:SYNTHESIS-EVIDENCE',['p91','p93','p95','p97'],'Shared covariance then carries information that independent private fluctuations cannot supply','Covariance supports a shared fluctuation component under the decomposition assumptions.','covariance comparison','shared and private components','distinguishes evidence available from joint responses','the decomposition’s assumptions must hold','retain','“Carries information” has a clear statistical object here and is immediately qualified; the phrase is not an unexplained transport metaphor.','The three tests differ: extra spatial summaries, calibrated displacement covariance, and an inequality with compatible estimates. The conditions prevent treating 1/N scaling as a full bound test.','Fisher information, MSD, diffusion and calibration have prior teaching; do not rename them to satisfy repetition checks.','The shared-position calculation motivates what measurements are missing before each paper’s evidence is compared.','Each model needs a test matched to its claim states the governing criterion.','The list’s parallel form enables comparison on a common evidence question.')
assess('06-synthesis.md','sec:SYNTHESIS-RELATED',['p103','p105','p107','p109','p111'],'Structure and learning can therefore be present even when a random-function model describes many aggregate field statistics.','A statistical fit does not decide which circuit produced it.','structured connections and synaptic learning','spatial rate maps','can produce maps compatible with aggregate random-function statistics','the summary statistics do not uniquely identify circuit construction','retain','The transition follows concrete connectivity and plasticity studies, so it makes a supported connection rather than adding filler.','Each study group changes a specific assumption or evidence source. Retain the reanalysis and later-study chronology, and the difference between perceptual benefit and generator.','Path integration and dendrite have local blue definitions. Paper titles retain their exact wording and author initials retain their actual forms.','The source model and its limits come before related work tests those assumptions.','The heading states the effect of these studies on circuit choices.','The final generator limitation returns the reader to what a joint experiment needs to distinguish.')
assess('06-synthesis.md','sec:SYNTHESIS-NEXT',['p115','p117','p118','p119','p120','p122'],'a mismatch would point to a particular assumption to change','A failed joint comparison needs further tests to locate the cause.','proposed measurements and follow-up tests','spatial input, maintenance, observation and coupling assumptions','compare and investigate','a mismatch alone does not choose one assumption','revise','Name the measurements and give the comparison reference for “more restrictive.” Keep the four candidate causes without implying unique diagnosis.','The numbered actions are genuine proposed experimental steps, so imperative style is appropriate. The static-versus-diffusion distinctions prevent either isolated fit from counting as the joint test.','All listed quantities have earlier teaching; no new method is introduced in the proposal.','Map estimation precedes alignment and diffusion fitting; downstream filters are conditional on comparing behavior.','The heading names the two measured objects to compare.','The closing label keeps this proposed work separate from a claimed replication.')
assess('glossary.md','ch:GLOSSARY',['p3','p22','p25','p34','p52','p70','p89'],'A representation carried by the pattern of responses across neurons.','The population response pattern represents a value.','neural response pattern','represented value','expresses the code across neurons','lookup after the main teaching','retain','The familiar phrase identifies the representational object without claiming physical transport. Add displacement and split the identified prose semicolons.','Short entries are useful lookup definitions after linked chapter teaching. Full derivations would duplicate that teaching and impede lookup. Keep technical assumptions in entries such as Poisson and stationary process.','The existing 97 entries use the body spellings; displacement is the confirmed missing 98th term. Kac–Rice and left zero eigenvector are exact names.','This is a lookup aid rather than a prerequisite substitute; the opening says so.','Glossary is a reference heading, so a contribution claim would be inappropriate.','Alphabetical entries do not need invented narrative transitions.')
